{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_http_endpoints_management_http_endpoints", "label": "Management HTTP endpoints", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/management/http-endpoints.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_http_endpoints_health_endpoint", "label": "GET /health", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/management/http-endpoints.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_http_endpoints_ready_endpoint", "label": "GET /ready", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/management/http-endpoints.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_http_endpoints_cluster_members_endpoint", "label": "GET /cluster/members", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/management/http-endpoints.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Full membership snapshot - manual state checks during incidents, external dashboards, and tests verifying cluster joining."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_http_endpoints_cluster_leader_endpoint", "label": "GET /cluster/leader", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/management/http-endpoints.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The leader address plus whether the local node is it; null before a leader is elected."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_http_endpoints_cluster_shards_endpoint", "label": "GET /cluster/shards", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/management/http-endpoints.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Shard-to-region allocation for a sharded type - verifying even distribution after a rebalance, diagnosing hot regions, manual rebalance triggers in development."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_http_endpoints_metrics_endpoint", "label": "GET /metrics", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/management/http-endpoints.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_http_endpoints_cluster_leave_endpoint", "label": "POST /cluster/leave", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/management/http-endpoints.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Opt-in and one-way: the node transitions through leaving, exiting and removed, shards rebalance away, and it cannot rejoin in the same process. Gate behind authentication - anyone with port access can drain your node."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_http_endpoints_cluster_down_endpoint", "label": "POST /cluster/down", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/management/http-endpoints.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Opt-in, destructive and irrecoverable: the target actors stop and its shards reallocate elsewhere. For split-brain recovery with no downing strategy configured, and for removing stuck unreachable members. Gate behind auth plus audit logs."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_http_endpoints_auth_and_ip_allowlist", "label": "Management auth and IP allowlisting", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/management/http-endpoints.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The privileged endpoints accept anonymous requests by default, which is only safe on a network-isolated bind or behind an authenticating proxy. The policy split is deliberate: auth wraps the privileged subset and leaves health and ready anonymous because Kubernetes probes cannot easily attach an Authorization header, while ipAllowlist wraps every endpoint because network-level isolation is independent of who is authenticated."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_http_endpoints_management_response_format", "label": "Management response format", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/management/http-endpoints.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Reads and the down endpoint return JSON, metrics returns Prometheus text, leave returns the plain-text word leaving; errors are plain-text bodies, and the admin actions answer 202 Accepted."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_http_endpoints_management_topology_disclosure", "label": "Read-only endpoints still reveal topology", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/management/http-endpoints.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Member addresses, roles, the leader and the shard map are internal topology, so the management server is sensitive even where nothing is mutable: bind it to an internal interface and gate it rather than exposing it publicly."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_http_endpoints_managem